      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 104</b></color></size>\n<b>The 'Pashupati' seal</b>\n<size=74%>c. 2350\u20132000 BCE\n<i>Steatite, about 3.5 cm square</i>\nNational Museum, New Delhi</size>\n<size=70%><line-height=110%>\nIndus seals were pressed into clay to mark goods. This one shows a horned figure seated cross-legged, surrounded by an elephant, a tiger, a rhinoceros and a buffalo. Early scholars linked the figure to the god Shiva as 'lord of animals', but its meaning is still debated.</size>"
