      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 101</b></color></size>

    <b>Rock paintings of Bhimbetka</b>

    <size=74%>Mesolithic period onwards (from c. 10,000 BCE)

    <i>Natural mineral pigments on sandstone</i>

    In situ, Bhimbetka rock shelters, Madhya Pradesh (UNESCO World Heritage Site)</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    More than 750 rock shelters in the Vindhya hills hold paintings of hunters, dancers, horses, elephants and wild cattle, made with red and white mineral pigments. The oldest layers are thought to date from the Mesolithic period, making them among the earliest known art in India.</size>'
